From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Sun, 11 Oct 2026 16:50:47 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Preview: pictures that stay put, the rating backing inside
 the card, the club code only for a missing badge (Parker, 11 Oct 2026)

Parker, 11 Oct 2026, on his iPhone during GW6, with a screenshot of a player sheet: "The images are still disappearing
sporadically when I click into someone and when I scroll and what's this weird artifact by the rating area? Also some
weird text poking through under the man city and Liverpool mini bubbles there."

- BUGS #49: a live refresh redrew the page and the open sheet with innerHTML and threw every picture away (0 of 15 and
  0 of 18 kept after one reload). src/swap.js swapHTML keeps every loaded <img> (15 of 15, 18 of 18); no filter on the
  Plate photos; the sheet's Plate decodes its photo before it paints.
- BUGS #50: the rating's backing reached the card's top edge and stuck out of its cut corner; it starts inside the
  inner keyline now, its corner cut parallel to the card's, still covering the band the contrast audit reads. The light
  beam behind the sheet's Plate fades out instead of ending in a line.
- BUGS #51: the club code under a badge poked out at both sides; it shows only when the badge is missing or fails.

Tests: tests/app-images.js (new), tests/app-contrast.js P3 and C16 updated; the browser half
fplgg/tools/preview/check-images.js. Every suite passes; the contrast audit with the real fonts finds 0 offenders on 42
screens. Run report: fplgg/tools/matchweek/docs/runs/2026-10-11-sheet-images.md

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01JTueX5iCoHHVi1DWjPjRYc
