+- **#49 P1: player photos blanked on live refreshes and on scroll (iPhone).** Parker, 11 Oct 2026, 16:27 UTC, GW6 live (LIV v MCI at 45'), with a screenshot of Ndiaye's sheet: "The images are still disappearing sporadically when I click into someone and when I scroll." Cause, reproduced in Chromium on the built demo: while a match is on the app reloads every 90 s and `render` and `refreshSheet` (`src/main.js`) redrew the page and the open sheet with innerHTML, which threw away every `<img>`; after one `MW.reload` 0 of 15 pictures on the page and 0 of 18 in a player sheet were the same elements, so the phone fetched and decoded every photo, badge and flag again (the photos lazy or async, blank until decoded; on iOS sometimes until the next scroll). Two iOS costs on top: every Plate photo carried `filter: drop-shadow` (a compositing layer of its own per picture, thirty on a pitch; the same symptom on Rice in the old app was cured by dropping the sheet photo's filter), and the sheet's big Plate decoded its photo asynchronously as it slid in. Closed 11 Oct 2026, manager, on the `preview` branch: `src/swap.js` `swapHTML` moves each loaded picture into the matching slot of the new markup (same src; the new attributes copied over; src never set again), used for the page and the sheet (after one reload: 15 of 15 and 18 of 18 kept); `.fc .face img{filter:none}`; the sheet's Plate decodes synchronously. Tests: `tests/app-images.js`; browser half `fplgg/tools/preview/check-images.js`. Not reproducible off an iPhone: Parker's phone is the final check.
+- **#50 P2: the rating's backing stuck out of the Plate.** Parker, same screenshot: "what's this weird artifact by the rating area". The high-contrast pass (10 Oct) gave the rating a backing box reaching 6% of the card's width above the figure: its top sat at 3.8 cqw, on the card's top edge (4.0) and over its inner keyline (6.31), and its square corner stuck out past the card's cut top left corner. Closed 11 Oct 2026, manager, on the `preview` branch: the backing is `.fc .rt::before`, starting at 7.3 cqw (inside the keyline), its top left corner cut parallel to the card's; it still covers the band of the figure the contrast audit reads (from 8.2 cqw with Saira Condensed). The contrast audit passes on the demo with the real fonts (0 offenders, 42 screens). Also: the light beam behind the sheet's Plate ended in a hard line beside the card; it fades out now (`.ps-beam` mask).
+- **#51 P2: the club code poked out beside the badge in the sheet's chips.** Parker, same screenshot: "some weird text poking through under the man city and Liverpool mini bubbles". `cb` (`src/sheets/kit.js`) put the club code under the badge as a fallback; "MCI" is 21 px wide in an 18 px circle around a 13 px badge, so its letters showed at both sides. Closed 11 Oct 2026, manager, on the `preview` branch: the circle is marked `im` while it holds a badge and the code is hidden there (`.sk-cb.im em`); the badge's own error handler takes the mark off, so a failed badge still shows the code. Everywhere `cb` is used (the player and manager sheets' chips and lists).
